*(Repost to the public discuss list of a note originally sent to the
keyholders list on 2026-08-15; lightly redacted for the public archive.)*

Hello Bus friends!

Ripley and I will be working on the bus this afternoon, focusing on
waterproofing the body and orifices. :-)

- Feel free to come by, we have fiberglass, caulk and some related tools;
  I'll be taking measurements for some of any wonky shapes that may need
  prints / inserts made.
- If you have sheet metal, sheet plastic etc feel free to drop it by.

I will come up with an interim lock solution today to implement by the end
of the coming week. I am planning on working on bus stuff Thursdays and
Fridays ~3pm-5pm ish ish.

Things the bus could benefit from soonish:

- 9/16 impact / large breaker for the stubborn bolt(s) (so far only one has
  really screwed me over)
- Cleaning supplies (I have brought and left contractor bags and black
  gloves); a broom / industrial cleaner + rags could go a long way
- A set of imperial square bits up to ⅞"
- A set of SecurityTorx bits / drivers plz
- Social media skills / make noise about bus things

Things on my docket:

- Grab posters from Alex, post in bus and integrate into an interim single
  page application with Alex's form, near term membership and project
  objectives, needs, some info about the project, timeline, my planned
  working hours and static log. Will have this live by the end of the
  weekend at greatfallstoolbus.org.

Things I'd love help with:

- Workshoping the user stories for member onboarding, tool checkout, tool
  repair and tool check in, leaving the org, donating tools or resources to
  the org etc; If anyone wants to hang out sometime next week or at 5th
  pillar to work through how we want to make these processes as slick and
  simple as possible, plz let me know! This can be a tedious process but is
  fun with friends
- UX, branding, design, asset (logo, fonts, palette, icon) creation
- Writing templatable copy for user onboarding

Next few weeks for Jess:

- I'll be mostly focused on getting the membership related infrastructure /
  CRM operations in place as outlined in my last email. This includes user
  provisioning (member status, email provisioning, inventory MVP and its
  associated web application, member lifecycle) as well as the tool
  acquisition lifecycle and tool schema (what gets checked out by who, what
  is checked out with it, entity semaphore, manage consumables / docs /
  liability per tool, where it goes, when it comes back etc)
  - The mid term intent as discussed with Alex is to manage all this through
    the tooling available through user's smartphones (location, camera for
    checkout and check in for contents, take out and return flow can all be
    done with the glory of modern mobile browser owo); not all this will be
    done by mid September.

Seat and interior work notes:

- We need hands removing and preparing seats for out-of-bus seat duty!
- I have removed 3 seats thusly and fully removed all the rear most
  passenger side bench fasteners, ready to be removed (do not sit on it ^w^)
- I have left a socket + square bit that handles the seat bottom plastic
  bits for seat removal, as well as smol ½ and 3/16" sockets, ratchet and
  open end wrenches.

Other notes:

- The drive axle bolts are in the white bag at the front of the bus
  currently, I'll label these
- The one with the ziptie is for the driver side

I have gathered a large amount of photos and some GPS data and plot data,
which I'd be glad to share with y'all eventually for mockup purposes in CAD.

I am keen to have a meeting re. asset agreement and liability structure
future proofing, I am keen to ensure we are boxing things up such that the
bus's structural trappings are indeed free of strings / future webs; I
understand we are aiming currently to be established under a fiscal sponsor,
and want to make sure organizational liability and transferability when the
future of organizational entanglement comes to pass. ^w^

How about next Thursday the 20th at 4pm at the teahouse?

Cheers,
-Jess
